# Host invariants the repo expects BEYOND what its own files set.
#
# scripts/vpn-bot-host-check derives the sysctl, sshd and systemd *.conf keys to check
# from the repo files of the host's role on its own (MANAGED_HOST_FILES) — add a file
# there and its keys are checked. This list is for what no repo file carries.
#
# Format, one entry per line ('#' starts a comment line):
#   <role>|<probe>|<key>|<expected>|<reason, at least 20 characters>
# role      main | relay | all
# probe     a closed set — no arbitrary commands:
#   sshd                  key = sshd keyword; compared with `sshd -T`
#   sysctl                key = sysctl key; compared with `sysctl -n`
#   systemd-conf:<x>      x = journald|networkd|resolved|logind|timesyncd|system;
#                         key = Section.Key; compared with what the files give
#   unit-prop:<unit>:<P>  key = -; `systemctl show -p <P> <unit>` (several lines joined)
#   path-present          key = path; expected = -
#   path-absent           key = path; expected = -
#   path-regular          key = path; exists and is NOT a symlink; expected = -
#   tcp-listen:<port>     key = -; something listens on TCP <port>; expected = -
# expected  the value; "~X" = contains X as a whole token ("~22" matches
#           "[::]:22 (Stream)", not ":2222"); "-" where the probe needs none.
# A line that does not hold is a MISMATCH: fatal in deploy Phase 1, a rollback in
# Phase 2, an alert to the superadmins on the main server.
# tests/test_host_check.py checks every line (probe set, field count, reason length).

# The SSH port is not here: it follows SSH_PORT in .env on both roles, and the host
# check judges it from that (family ssh-port, docs/host-state.md#the-ssh-port) — a
# fixed port in this list would contradict the setting during and after a migration.

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------------
main|unit-prop:even-day-reboot.timer:UnitFileState|-|enabled|the scheduled reboot is how kernel and library updates take effect; a disabled timer silently stops them
main|unit-prop:even-day-reboot.timer:ActiveState|-|active|an enabled timer that is not running schedules nothing until the next boot
main|path-regular|/etc/resolv.conf|-|the main server resolves through a plain resolv.conf from the repo (deploy/host/dns/resolv.conf), not resolved's stub symlink

# --- relay ---------------------------------------------------------------------
relay|unit-prop:ufw.service:UnitFileState|-|masked|the relay's INPUT filter is table inet vpnrelay_input (vpn-relay-apply); UFW's own forward chain (policy DROP) is a second base chain on the forward hook and would drop the relayed 443 whatever table ip vpnrelay says

# --- both roles ----------------------------------------------------------------
all|path-present|/etc/cloud/cloud-init.disabled|-|cloud-init must stay off: on a reboot it rewrote sshd_config.d and sudoers.d behind the repo's back
